From 053ff674a48f79e6ee414f4da7135aff3437099a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:21:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Support the ARM IOMMU DMA backend

Native 32-bit Qualcomm platforms use ARM_DMA_USE_IOMMU rather than
IOMMU_DMA. Allow that backend without relaxing ARCH_QCOM or changing the
existing COMPILE_TEST alternative.

ARM's IOMMU mapper merges input entries only up to the device's maximum
segment size, which defaults to 64 KiB. Larger images can therefore map
to separately allocated DMA ranges with gaps between them. VFE write
masters consume a base address per plane and cannot follow those gaps.

Raise the maximum segment size before registering capture devices. Check
that adjacent mapped DMA segments cover sizeimage before accepting a
buffer. Permit adjacent segments and an unused noncontiguous tail rather
than requiring exactly one segment or rejecting oversized imports.
Keep the existing single-plane NV chroma address calculation unchanged.

Fold the DMA prerequisite into the ARM32 feature introduction. This
refreshes integration changes 9d46e4575ea1 and 8fe23bfec791, and replaces
the Kconfig-only proposal 2f2e63bfa290 on media-committers next.

A host model executes the actual ARM mapper, platform DMA defaults,
DMA parameter helpers and CAMSS buffer initialization/preparation. Its
synthetic IOVA allocator leaves gaps between separately mapped chunks.
The model has 14 failed checks before this change and none afterward;
removing the segment limit or range guard causes failures. It also
checks adjacent imports, sufficient contiguous prefixes, plane isolation,
chroma offsets and mapper failures. It does not execute the full probe,
real VB2 allocation, hardware DMA or image capture. Native ARM and ARM64
CAMSS components build with W=1 and no new warnings. Physical V4L2
compliance and camera integrity remain pending.

The original changes by Timothy Schmidt were developed with Claude Opus
5.5, credited as a co-author <noreply@anthropic.com> in their history.
OpenAI Codex (GPT-6) adapted the current feature and range checks, wrote
the host model, and performed local build and regression qualification.
Human review and DCO certification remain pending.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig     |  2 +-
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c   | 23 ++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c     |  3 +++
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig
index b51745c942..abb63aebe5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/Kconfig
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ config VIDEO_QCOM_CAMSS
 	tristate "Qualcomm V4L2 Camera Subsystem driver"
 	depends on V4L_PLATFORM_DRIVERS
 	depends on VIDEO_DEV
-	depends on (ARCH_QCOM && IOMMU_DMA) || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on (ARCH_QCOM && (IOMMU_DMA || ARM_DMA_USE_IOMMU)) || COMPILE_TEST
 	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
 	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
 	select VIDEOBUF2_DMA_SG
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
index 0852eb6f13..c6a576ba18 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
@@ -155,13 +155,34 @@ static int video_buf_init(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	const struct v4l2_pix_format_mplane *format =
 						&video->active_fmt.fmt.pix_mp;
 	struct sg_table *sgt;
-	unsigned int i;
+	struct scatterlist *s;
+	dma_addr_t expected;
+	unsigned long size;
+	unsigned int i, j;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < format->num_planes; i++) {
 		sgt = vb2_dma_sg_plane_desc(vb, i);
 		if (!sgt)
 			return -EFAULT;
 
+		/* Adjacent DMA segments may cover one linear image plane. */
+		expected = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
+		size = 0;
+		for_each_sgtable_dma_sg(sgt, s, j) {
+			if (sg_dma_address(s) != expected)
+				break;
+			size += sg_dma_len(s);
+			if (size >= format->plane_fmt[i].sizeimage)
+				break;
+			expected += sg_dma_len(s);
+		}
+		if (size < format->plane_fmt[i].sizeimage) {
+			dev_err_ratelimited(video->camss->dev,
+					    "Buffer plane %u is not contiguous\n",
+					    i);
+			return -EFAULT;
+		}
+
 		buffer->addr[i] = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index c54185c93a..8c76e8a193 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5478,6 +5478,9 @@ static int camss_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_genpd_cleanup;
 
+	/* VFE write masters need a linear DMA range per image plane. */
+	dma_set_max_seg_size(dev, UINT_MAX);
+
 	camss->media_dev.dev = camss->dev;
 	strscpy(camss->media_dev.model, "Qualcomm Camera Subsystem",
 		sizeof(camss->media_dev.model));
-- 
